4],[1746057600,20.16],[1748736000,18.95],[1751328000,19.97],[1754006400,20.97],[1756684800,23.29],[1759276800,27.85],[1761955200,19.95],[1764547200,19.94],[1767225600,18.88],[1769904000,20.63],[1772323200,25.79],[1775001600,17.68],[1777593600,26.46],[1780272000,29.86],[1782864000,31.85],[1785542400,32.18]]}]}],"qna":[{"question":"What does the Foodgrain Stocks Data represent?","answer":"The Foodgrain Stocks data represents the quantity of food grains such as wheat, rice, and other cereals, held in reserves by the government or related entities at a given time.^These stocks are typically maintained as a strategic reserve to ensure food security, stabilise foodgrain prices, and manage emergency situations.^The data reflects the accumulated outcome of past agricultural production and procurement policies."},{"question":"What is the significance of Foodgrains Stocks data?","answer":"Foodgrain Stocks serve as a buffer against food shortages, price volatility, and are used for food security purposes.^The size of foodgrain stocks can be an indicator of the agricultural sector's output, particularly in terms of surplus production beyond immediate consumption and export demands.^Large stocks are often seen as a buffer against potential food shortages, ensuring a steady supply for domestic consumption, especially in times of crop failure or market fluctuations.^The level of foodgrain stocks can influence market prices for grains. Adequate stocks tend to stabilise prices, while low stocks might lead to price spikes.^The data provides insights into the effectiveness of agricultural and food procurement policies. It reflects the government's capacity to procure from farmers and manage the supply chain."},{"question":"How to interpret the Foodgrains Stocks data?","answer":"Rising stocks might indicate increased production or procurement, while declining stocks could signal reduced output or higher offtake.^The seasonality of agricultural production and procurement cycles should be considered. For instance, post-harvest periods typically see an increase in stocks.^In the context of global agricultural markets, consider how domestic stock levels compare with international trends and their potential impact on export-import dynamics.^The data can be used to evaluate the need for policy adjustments, such as incentives for crop diversification, improvements in storage infrastructure, or changes in export-import policies.^Compare current stock levels against historical data to understand trends. The current state of foodgrain stocks can inform predictions about future market conditions, potential export opportunities, and the need for imports."}],"related":[{"slug":"annual-rainfall-lpa","title":"Annual Rainfall (% of LPA)"},{"slug":"consumer-price-index-cpi-inflation-food","title":"Consumer Price Index (CPI) Inflation - Food"},{"slug":"consumer-price-index-cpi-inflation-food-rural","title":"Consumer Price Index (CPI) Inflation - Food Rural"},{"slug":"consumer-price-index-cpi-inflation-miscellaneous-rural","title":"Consumer Price Index (CPI) Inflation- Miscellaneous Rural"},{"slug":"domestic-tractor-sales","title":"Domestic Tractor Sales"},{"slug":"exports-agricultural-allied-products","title":"Exports - Agricultural & Allied Products"},{"slug":"fertiliser-sales","title":"Fertiliser Sales"},{"slug":"kharif-sowing-progress","title":"Kharif Sowing Progress"},{"slug":"rabi-sowing-progress","title":"Rabi Sowing Progress"},{"slug":"reservoir-level-10-year-average","title":"Reservoir Level (vs 10Y Avg)"},{"slug":"south-west-monsoon-rainfall-deviation-from-normal","title":"South-west Monsoon Rainfall: Deviation from Normal"},{"slug":"wholesale-price-index-wpi-inflation-food","title":"Wholesale Price Index (WPI) Inflation - Food"}],"title":"Foodgrain Stocks","description":"India's foodgrain stocks stand at 108.3 Million Tonnes for Aug 2026. Stock levels against buffer norms show how much room the government has to intervene in food markets.","headline":{"Absolute":"India's foodgrain stocks stand at 108.3 Million Tonnes for Aug 2026. Stock levels against buffer norms show how much room the government has to intervene in food markets.","Y-o-Y":"India's foodgrain stocks stand at 32.18% for Aug 2026. Stock levels against buffer norms show how much room the government has to intervene in food markets."},"source":"CMIE Economic Outlook, 1 Finance Research","source_url":"https://economicoutlook.cmie.com/","date_modified":"2026-08-01","scraped_at":"2026-10-13T15:27:50+00:00"}